\details{
Typed, event-driven client for Binance's \strong{public} spot market-data streams.
Inherits the Node.js-style event API and connection management from
\link{BinanceWsBase} (\verb{$on()}, \verb{$subscribe()}, \verb{$run()}, auto-reconnect). No API key
is required — these are public streams.

Many symbols ride a single connection (Binance allows up to 1024 streams per
connection), so subscribing to 100 order books is one socket, not 100.
\subsection{Streams Covered}{\tabular{lll}{
   Method \tab Stream \tab Auth \cr
   depth \tab \verb{<symbol>@depth} / \verb{<symbol>@depth@100ms} \tab No \cr
}


Handlers receive the \strong{raw JSON message string} (parse with
\code{\link[jsonlite:fromJSON]{jsonlite::fromJSON()}}, or write it straight to disk for archival). The
\verb{@depth} stream is the full diff stream — every order-book change — from which
the complete book can be reconstructed; reconstruction is a separate concern
(a future helper), this class faithfully captures the stream.
}
}
